  "notes": "v302: REVENUE-LEARNS-PAY-CYCLE (owner, Oct 31, 2026) — Revenue now LEARNS the driver's pay rhythm from his own invoicing history (issued + settled invoice periods and pay-stub periods) instead of making him fight a calendar picker. Semi-monthly is one candidate among four (semi-monthly / monthly / weekly / biweekly), learned only when at least two distinct periods follow it and they are a strict majority of the distinct periods on record — nothing is hard-coded, a weekly-paid driver learns weekly, and a sparse or split history learns nothing and keeps the manual behaviour untouched. With a rhythm learned: Revenue opens framed on the CURRENT learned period (for Asjad, Nov 1–15), past learned periods are one-tap chips (capped at four), a hand-picked custom range snaps out to whole learned periods, and the face prints the rule in plain words (“Learned from your invoices: you invoice on the 15th and month-end”) with the open period's expected payday (“Oct 16–31 · paid ~Nov 1”). The rule is stored per work profile and re-learned on every render, so a newly issued invoice teaches it at once; a rhythm already learned never re-seizes the view from a pick he made himself. Totals ride the same shared builder as always — October reconciles to his own recording exactly ($6,864.21 · 74 loads).",
